WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.850
An AI servicing agent wants to take a
consequential action: schedule a foreclosure

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:07.200
hearing for September twenty-fourth.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.533
The model behind it may be confident.

00:00:09.533 --> 00:00:12.747
NorthCannon does not treat
that confidence as evidence.

00:00:12.747 --> 00:00:15.130
It verifies the decision itself.

00:00:16.253 --> 00:00:21.708
It checks the evidence, the governing
rule, time, authority, and the current case

00:00:21.708 --> 00:00:25.516
state. Earliest permitted
date: September eighteenth.

00:00:25.516 --> 00:00:28.264
Proposed: the twenty-fourth.

00:00:28.264 --> 00:00:30.504
Supported. Proceed.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.308
Now let's see why this was allowed.

00:00:33.308 --> 00:00:38.305
Every decision keeps why it was trusted:
the evidence, the rule, and the date

00:00:38.305 --> 00:00:39.305
arithmetic.

00:00:40.226 --> 00:00:43.480
Starting foreclosure creates
an obligation of its own.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:49.347
Foreclosure was initiated September eighth,
so a HUD foreclosure-initiation notice

00:00:49.347 --> 00:00:53.330
is due within thirty calendar
days: October eighth.

00:00:55.384 --> 00:01:00.547
When that notice is missed, NorthCannon
shows a concrete claim consequence,

00:01:00.547 --> 00:01:06.427
interest curtailment. Separately,
it shows a regulatory exposure that

00:01:06.427 --> 00:01:10.330
stays conditional. The two are
never treated as the same thing.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:16.880
The same architecture works in
a different regulated domain.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.500
A commercial-credit application at
Harbor National Bank, a fictional demo

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:27.130
institution, is in scope for section ten
seventy-one small-business reporting.

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:33.240
Then the rule changes. Regulation
B's small-business threshold

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.813
drops, from five million
dollars to one million.

00:01:36.813 --> 00:01:40.540
NorthCannon knows which
determinations depended on it.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:43.308
One of four applications is affected.

00:01:43.308 --> 00:01:46.932
Three are unchanged, and are not re-run.

00:01:47.522 --> 00:01:51.358
And in the behavior we're building,
the change reaches further.

00:01:51.358 --> 00:01:57.422
Five of ten downstream models, metrics,
rules, and reports were built on the

00:01:57.422 --> 00:02:03.302
old rule version. Open one, and it shows
exactly which parts are outdated, and which

00:02:03.302 --> 00:02:04.472
are still current.

00:02:05.541 --> 00:02:10.681
Re-evaluated: two point four million
dollars is above the new threshold.

00:02:10.681 --> 00:02:13.941
Out of scope, under the
selected rule version.

00:02:13.941 --> 00:02:18.111
That's a classification change,
not a judgment about the applicant.

00:02:20.128 --> 00:02:25.358
It also opens an action: remove this
application from the section ten seventy-one

00:02:25.358 --> 00:02:29.352
reporting stage. It stays
in the commercial pipeline.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:35.170
When the pipeline is updated, NorthCannon
verifies the result before it closes the

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.170
action.

00:02:36.881 --> 00:02:42.181
The original determination is preserved,
dated to the rule it was decided under.

00:02:42.181 --> 00:02:44.901
It was supported on what was known then.

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:46.631
It is not rewritten.

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:51.557
And it isn't limited to
regulated industries.

00:02:51.557 --> 00:02:55.845
Here the same engine is pointed at a
fictional demo company's supply chain.

00:02:55.845 --> 00:03:00.601
This is illustrative: designed
behavior, not yet implemented.

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:05.441
One rule change, and three of five
dependent assets are affected.

00:03:05.441 --> 00:03:10.832
The same question every time: which
prior decisions depended on what changed?

00:03:12.858 --> 00:03:15.270
Verified the decision before action.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:17.489
Preserved why it was trusted.

00:03:17.489 --> 00:03:19.862
Detected when its support changed.

00:03:19.862 --> 00:03:22.760
Re-evaluated only what was affected.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:27.962
Mortgage servicing, commercial lending,
and supply chain are proving grounds.

00:03:27.962 --> 00:03:32.648
The layer sits between machine
intelligence and any consequential action.

00:03:32.648 --> 00:03:37.632
NorthCannon: trust infrastructure
for machine intelligence.
